text:
{
  "milestones": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "add check_imaginary to Arrow.shift",
      "requests": [
        "R6"
      ],
      "requirement": "I want Arrow.shift to accept a check_imaginary parameter, defaulting to True, so I can explicitly skip DST/imaginary-time adjustment when I know it is unnecessary.",
      "observable": "Arrow.fromdatetime(datetime(2023, 2, 12, 2, 30), tzinfo='US/Eastern').shift(months=1) returns an Arrow whose hour is 3, preserving the existing imaginary-time adjustment; the same shift called with check_imaginary=False returns an Arrow whose hour is 2; calls with no check_imaginary still behave as before.",
      "public_names": [
        "Arrow.shift",
        "check_imaginary"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "why_requires": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "title": "use shift check_imaginary for humanize month limits",
      "requests": [
        "R5"
      ],
      "requirement": "I want humanize month limits to be correct at calendar month boundaries, including when the month-boundary calculation would otherwise adjust an imaginary DST time, by using Arrow.shift with check_imaginary=False for the boundary comparison.",
      "observable": "arrow.get(2023, 1, 1).humanize(arrow.get(2023, 2, 1)) == 'in a month' and arrow.get(2023, 1, 1).humanize(arrow.get(2023, 3, 1)) == 'in 2 months'. For the DST month boundary, Arrow.fromdatetime(datetime(2023, 2, 12, 2, 30), tzinfo='US/Eastern').humanize(Arrow.fromdatetime(datetime(2023, 3, 12, 2, 30), tzinfo='US/Eastern')) == 'in a month'. A hidden test wraps Arrow.shift to record kwargs and calls humanize on the DST boundary; it expects the wrapper to record check_imaginary=False and expects the returned string. Without m1, forwarding the recorded call to the original Arrow.shift raises TypeError.",
      "public_names": [
        "Arrow.humanize"
      ],
      "requires": [
        "m1"
      ],
      "why_requires": "Arrow.humanize's month-limit calculation calls Arrow.shift with the check_imaginary parameter added in m1."
    }
  ],
  "expected_causes": [
    "Implementing the month-limit fix with calendar or timedelta arithmetic only, so Arrow.humanize never calls Arrow.shift and the required dependency is not exercised.",
    "Choosing a DST example where the adjusted and unadjusted boundary both yield the same humanized string.",
    "Adding check_imaginary with the wrong default, such as False, breaking existing shift behavior.",
    "Calling Arrow.shift with check_imaginary=True in humanize, leaving imaginary-time adjustment to corrupt month limits.",
    "Writing a monkeypatch test that only checks the returned string but does not assert that Arrow.shift was called with check_imaginary=False."
  ],
  "verifier_plan": "Hidden tests for m1 call Arrow.shift on normal and DST-imaginary dates, assert that check_imaginary is accepted, assert default True behavior remains unchanged, and assert check_imaginary=False skips the imaginary-time adjustment. Hidden tests for m2 first assert ordinary month-boundary humanize strings. Then they monkeypatch Arrow.shift with a recording wrapper that forwards to the original method, call Arrow.humanize on the DST month-boundary case, assert the wrapper recorded check_imaginary=False, and assert the exact returned humanized string. If m1 is absent, the forwarded call to the original Arrow.shift with check_imaginary raises TypeError, so m2 cannot pass without m1."
}
